# Since the ".env" file is gitignored, you can use the ".env.example" file to
# build a new ".env" file when you clone the repo. Keep this file up-to-date
# when you add new variables to `.env`.

# This file will be committed to version control, so make sure not to have any
# secrets in it. If you are cloning this repo, create a copy of this file named
# ".env" and populate it with your secrets.

# When adding additional environment variables, the schema in "/src/env.js"
# should be updated accordingly.

# Drizzle — the multiplayer store lives in Postgres (Neon over neon-http).
# A libsql/sqlite `file:` URL will NOT work with the neon-http driver.
# Fetch a real connection string for the branch you want (dev for local work):
#   neonctl connection-string dev --project-id muddy-night-85782525
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# AI opponents ("Versus AI" mode) — server-side only, never sent to clients.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is required to seat an AI player. ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL is
# optional: point it at an Anthropic-compatible gateway (e.g. OpenCode Zen,
# https://opencode.ai/zen) when the key belongs to one. With a gateway,
# model aliases (claude-haiku-4-5) work but dated ids may not.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-..."
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL="https://opencode.ai/zen"
# The budget tier ("The Clerk", minimax-m3) is gateway-only: it needs
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and is called over the OpenAI-compatible wire.
# BB_AI_MOCK=1 replaces the model with a deterministic mock (tests/e2e).

# Example:
# SERVERVAR="foo"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLIENTVAR="bar"
